Yes. This session cannot apply it: every tool call is blocked by the same broken hook. A working harness (plain PowerShell, or any agent whose hooks are not `conhost.exe`) can.

**What broke:** Claude/Cursor hook `command` is `C:\Windows\System32\conhost.exe`. The real Orca script is only in a non-standard `args` array (`--headless`, `cmd.exe`, `/d`, `/c`, `claude-hook.cmd`). Cursor and Claude Code execute **only** `command`, then pass the hook JSON as the process to launch. `conhost` treats that JSON as a filename → `The filename, directory name, or volume label syntax is incorrect` → invalid JSON → tools blocked.

**Known-good Cursor config:** `C:\Users\jeffk\.cursor\hooks.json.bak` (PowerShell → `C:\Users\jeffk\.orca\agent-hooks\cursor-hook.cmd`). Live `hooks.json` is missing.

Give this to a working harness. Run it in a **normal** PowerShell window, not inside this Cursor agent.

```powershell
#Requires -Version 5.1
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
$ts = Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd-HHmmss'

function Backup-IfExists([string]$Path) {
  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $Path) {
    $dest = "$Path.conhost-repair-$ts.bak"
    Copy-Item -LiteralPath $Path -Destination $dest -Force
    Write-Host "BACKED_UP $Path -> $dest"
  }
}

function Unwrap-Conhost([object]$Node) {
  $n = 0
  if ($null -eq $Node) { return 0 }
  if ($Node -is [System.Collections.IEnumerable] -and $Node -isnot [string]) {
    foreach ($item in @($Node)) { $n += Unwrap-Conhost $item }
    return $n
  }
  if ($Node -isnot [psobject]) { return 0 }
  $names = @($Node.PSObject.Properties.Name)
  if ($names -contains 'command') {
    $cmd = [string]$Node.command
    if ($cmd -match '(?i)conhost\.exe') {
      $replacement = $null
      if ($names -contains 'args' -and $Node.args) {
        $replacement = @(
          $Node.args |
            Where-Object { $_ -is [string] -and $_ -match '\.(cmd|bat|ps1|sh)$' }
        ) | Select-Object -Last 1
        if ($replacement) {
          $replacement = [Environment]::ExpandEnvironmentVariables([string]$replacement)
        }
      }
      if (-not $replacement) {
        $replacement = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '.orca\agent-hooks\claude-hook.cmd'
      }
      $Node.command = $replacement
      if ($names -contains 'args') {
        [void]$Node.PSObject.Properties.Remove('args')
      }
      $n++
    }
  }
  foreach ($p in $Node.PSObject.Properties) {
    if ($p.Name -in @('command', 'args')) { continue }
    $n += Unwrap-Conhost $p.Value
  }
  return $n
}

# --- Claude Code ---
$claude = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '.claude\settings.json'
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $claude)) { throw "Missing $claude" }
Backup-IfExists $claude
$claudeObj = Get-Content -LiteralPath $claude -Raw -Encoding UTF8 | ConvertFrom-Json
$claudeChanged = Unwrap-Conhost $claudeObj
($claudeObj | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 30) | Set-Content -LiteralPath $claude -Encoding UTF8
Write-Host "CLAUDE_UNWRAPPED $claudeChanged hooks in $claude"

# --- Cursor: restore known-good file, then unwrap if conhost still present ---
$cursorHooks = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '.cursor\hooks.json'
$cursorBak   = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE '.cursor\hooks.json.bak'
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $cursorBak) {
  Backup-IfExists $cursorHooks
  Copy-Item -LiteralPath $cursorBak -Destination $cursorHooks -Force
  Write-Host "CURSOR_RESTORED $cursorBak -> $cursorHooks"
} elseif (Test-Path -LiteralPath $cursorHooks) {
  Backup-IfExists $cursorHooks
} else {
  Write-Host "CURSOR_NO_HOOKS_FILE (check Cursor Settings > Hooks UI)"
}

if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $cursorHooks) {
  $raw = Get-Content -LiteralPath $cursorHooks -Raw -Encoding UTF8
  if ($raw -match '(?i)conhost\.exe') {
    $cursorObj = $raw | ConvertFrom-Json
    $cursorChanged = Unwrap-Conhost $cursorObj
    ($cursorObj | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 30) | Set-Content -LiteralPath $cursorHooks -Encoding UTF8
    Write-Host "CURSOR_UNWRAPPED $cursorChanged hooks in $cursorHooks"
  } else {
    Write-Host "CURSOR_CLEAN $cursorHooks"
  }
}

Write-Host '--- remaining conhost hits (must be 0) ---'
$hits = Select-String -Path @($claude, $cursorHooks) -Pattern 'conhost' -SimpleMatch -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
if ($hits) { $hits | Format-Table -AutoSize; throw 'conhost still present' }
Write-Host 'OK no conhost remains'
Write-Host 'NEXT: fully quit Cursor, reopen, start a NEW agent chat. This chat cannot recover.'
```

**Verify after restart**

- `C:\Users\jeffk\.claude\settings.json` hook `command` values are `...\orca\agent-hooks\claude-hook.cmd` with **no** `args` and **no** `conhost`.
- `C:\Users\jeffk\.cursor\hooks.json` exists and matches the `.bak` (PowerShell `EncodedCommand` → `cursor-hook.cmd`).
- Cursor Settings → Hooks shows that PowerShell command, not `conhost.exe`.
- A new agent chat can `Read` a file without `Hook "C:\Windows\System32\conhost.exe" returned invalid JSON`.

**Do not** wrap hooks in `conhost.exe --headless cmd.exe /d /c ...`. Cursor/Claude already spawn the command; `args` is not part of their hook schema, so only bare `conhost.exe` runs.

This current chat stays broken until Cursor is fully restarted. After that, Prodmax work can start at **T-001** (lowest open ticket, no unmet deps).

Copy everything below into a **working** agent (plain PowerShell, Orca, or a Cursor/Claude session whose hooks are **not** `conhost.exe`). Do not run it in the broken Cursor chat.

